{
  "title": "NeoSpan® Compression Implant System",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/implants/423278/neospan-r--compression-implant-system",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Dec 5 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The NeoSpan® Compression Implant System (CIS) is a product expansion of the NeoSpan® Compression Staple System.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423278/images/5ea7a57a-3b84-4d4e-9f76-e8ed62f57c59_screenshot_2025-09-11_at_12.35.49_pm.jpg",
              "caption": "NeoSpan® Compression Implant System (CIS)"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "It includes Nitinol implants in various configurations, such as Fixed-Leg and In-Line Implants with up to three screw holes, and T-Shape Implants with three legs and up to two screw holes.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Related Implants",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Fixed-Leg (In-Line)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Two fixed legs bridged by a bowed body; select variants incorporate one to three threaded screw holes (“+1H/+2H/+3H”).",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423278/images/464a057e-7f7a-4a98-8404-f646dee963af_screenshot_2025-09-11_at_12.16.34_pm_copy.jpg",
                  "caption": "Fixed-Leg and Inline Implants"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Threaded holes accept compatible 3.0 mm or 3.5 mm locking and non‑locking screws; all screws use a T15 driver.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "T-Shape",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Three fixed legs arranged in a T configuration, with up to two threaded screw holes for optional screw augmentation; accepts the same compatible screws (T15 driver).",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423278/images/eaff3627-b772-40ba-a561-6e2af0874625_screenshot_2025-09-11_at_12.16.41_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": "T-Shape Implant"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Indications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "NeoSpan® Compression Implant device is a nitinol implant intended to provide foot fixation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Fusions",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Osteotomies",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Osteology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Typical small‑bone targets include phalanges, metatarsals, and select tarsal bones.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Bony preparation aims to achieve flat, congruent fusion surfaces or stable osteotomy cuts prior to fixation.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Leg trajectory should remain within cortical confines; placement can be verified during trialing with K‑wires and fluoroscopy.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Muscles/Tendons",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Protect dorsal/plantar tendons in the foot through gentle retraction and avoidance of interposition at the fusion/osteotomy site.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ligaments/Capsule",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Exposure may require capsulotomy or ligament release; preserve or repair structures that contribute to adjacent joint stability.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Nerves",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Guard digital nerves in the dorsal cutaneous/plantar digital nerves in the foot during incision, K‑wire placement, and drilling.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Blood supply",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Minimize periosteal stripping; avoid injury to digital arteries and regional branches to support bone healing.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Approach",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Foot — incision",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Position supine with limb exsanguination and tourniquet as indicated.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Make a dorsal or medial incision according to the target fusion or osteotomy site (e.g., phalanx, metatarsal, midfoot).",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Protect dorsal cutaneous nerves and extensor tendons; confirm intended implant leg trajectory with a trial and fluoroscopy before opening the implant kit.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technique",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Trialing",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Open the Sterile Implant Trial Kit with K‑wires (T05 S0002).",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Use the trial to select configuration and size; K‑wires may hold the trial for fluoroscopic confirmation of placement and leg trajectory.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "After confirming, open the corresponding NeoSpan® CIS implant kit.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Note: trial markers indicate leg and screw‑hole positions relative to the trial’s reference line.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Prepare First Pilot Hole",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Using the provided calibrated drill and drill guide, prepare the first leg hole; reference the drill’s laser markings for depth.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423278/images/c30717ba-990d-46a3-868b-3aac59f738e6_screenshot_2025-09-11_at_11.29.33_am.jpg",
                  "caption": "Prepare first hole"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Without moving the guide, remove the drill and place a locator pin in the hole.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Prepare Other Pilot Hole(s)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Drill remaining hole(s) stepwise with the calibrated drill, again using laser markings for depth.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423278/images/48508688-fc9f-48ff-9976-01636008c6bb_screenshot_2025-09-11_at_11.31.39_am.jpg",
                  "caption": "Prepare other pilot hole(s)"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "For T‑shape configurations, place a second locator pin after the second hole to maintain guide position while preparing the final hole.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Prepare and Insert Implant",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Remove the implant/inserter assembly from the sterile kit (handle carefully; the implant is not fully secured to the inserter in the package).",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423278/images/1f7ac984-aaa1-4e8b-a616-82300c05c8f1_screenshot_2025-09-11_at_11.53.48_am.jpg",
                  "caption": "Prepare and insert implant"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Seat the implant firmly in the inserter prongs, then twist the handle clockwise to extend the internal plunger and spread the legs until they are parallel.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423278/images/9e05fa36-3add-43bc-b7c9-dc82ab9e1729_screenshot_2025-09-11_at_12.15.39_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": "Seat the implant firmly in the inserter prongs, then twist the handle clockwise to extend the internal plunger and spread the legs until they are parallel"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Align legs with pilot holes and advance with a mallet until the inserter prongs contact bone.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Important: legs must be parallel for proper insertion.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Release Implant and Remove Inserter",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Twist the inserter handle counter‑clockwise to retract the plunger and disengage from the implant.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423278/images/3a63b000-40e5-49e2-b4b4-f79871609c46_screenshot_2025-09-11_at_11.55.51_am.jpg",
                  "caption": "Release implant and remove inserter"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Slide the inserter away parallel to the bone surface and remove it.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423278/images/a5cfce51-98b2-463e-a847-b26b1024552d_screenshot_2025-09-11_at_12.39.01_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": "Slide the inserter away from the implant parallel to the bone surface"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Do not rock vertically to avoid lifting the implant.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Seat Implant",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "If needed, place inserter prongs on the implant’s top surface and gently tamp to ensure full seating.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423278/images/5f3a4176-89d8-421b-b931-b95908ae60d7_screenshot_2025-09-11_at_11.56.27_am.jpg",
                  "caption": "Seat implant"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "For configurations with threaded screw holes, achieve complete seating before any screw preparation.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Prepare Screw Insertion",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "For implants with threaded holes, open the sterile NeoSpan® Implant Screw Kit (T05 S0003).",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423278/images/d21aaaca-ced4-4869-a755-fabca6b6e8af_screenshot_2025-09-11_at_11.57.07_am.jpg",
                  "caption": "Prepare screw insertion"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Use the kit’s drill and guide to prepare each open hole; determine screw length with the depth gauge or by referencing calibrated drill markings.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Screw Placement",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Assemble the disposable AO Quick Connect Fixed Handle with the T15 driver from the screw kit.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423278/images/9c7fb06c-2e05-4707-a957-f09644887284_screenshot_2025-09-11_at_11.57.59_am.jpg",
                  "caption": "Screw placement"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Select the indicated 3.0 mm or 3.5 mm screw(s) and fully seat them into the prepared location(s).",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Closure",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Close by preferred methods.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Removal.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "If removal is desired, first remove all screws with the T15 driver.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Then remove the implant with an osteotome and/or the inserter instrument.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technical Specifications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Material & compression mechanics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Superelastic Nitinol implants arrive preloaded on an inserter in the Natural state; when deployed from the Active state, they return to a preformed bowed body that generates compression across the construct.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Barbed legs Implant legs incorporate a barbed feature to help resist pull‑out once implanted.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Implant legs incorporate a barbed feature to help resist pull‑out once implanted.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Threaded screw holes (select models)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Enable optional placement of screws for additional fixation; threaded holes are compatible with 3.0 mm and 3.5 mm locking/non‑locking screws.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Sizes & configurations",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Fixed‑Leg/In‑Line implants (two legs)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423278/images/2c0f0213-1174-478d-893f-6b2b2b3fe4fb_screenshot_2025-09-11_at_12.11.51_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": "Staple Style Implant"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "18 × 14 mm",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "18 × 16 mm",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "18 × 18 mm",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "20 × 20 mm",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "25 × 22 mm",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Fixed‑Leg/In‑Line implants +1H/+2H/+3H screw‑hole variants",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423278/images/c182156d-8737-4db9-a5aa-0d4e004feeb3_screenshot_2025-09-11_at_12.11.55_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": "+3 Hole Implant"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "18 × 14 mm",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "18 × 22 mm",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "T‑Shape implants are provided with 0–2 holes (three legs)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423278/images/26731297-32de-4290-acd3-448c17f2ae3c_screenshot_2025-09-11_at_12.12.08_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": "T-Shape (+2 Hole) Implant"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "T-shape",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "T-shape +1H",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "T-shape +2H",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Packaging & instruments",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "All implants are provided sterile.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "The system utilizes separate sterile instrument sets, including a Trial Kit for size determination and a Screw Kit with disposable instruments dedicated for screw implantation.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Screw material & driver",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Compatible screws are titanium alloy; all screws accept a T15 driver.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Screws",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Threaded Screw Holes — compatible with",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423278/images/624e53c1-4d0c-4365-979c-f5ba35e0591f_screenshot_2025-09-11_at_12.26.27_pm.jpg",
              "caption": "Threaded Screw Holes"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "3.0mm locking & non‑locking screws — lengths 10–30mm.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423278/images/61a4b524-3c9f-404b-a33e-d0242b021a11_screenshot_2025-09-11_at_12.31.59_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": "3.0mm locking & non-locking screws"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "3.5mm locking & non‑locking screws — lengths 10–40mm.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423278/images/5d3132ed-f0b8-413f-988b-0ac8911fb0ed_screenshot_2025-09-11_at_12.32.32_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": "3.5mm locking & non-locking screws"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "gallery": [
    {
      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423278/images/d9be3550-17d4-433d-81d2-fd06abf3cbfc_screenshot_2025-09-10_at_5.45.13_pm.jpg",
      "caption": ""
